      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NIGHT AND DAY (1) is a first starter from the Laurence Scala yard by Sunset Spitfire out of Sunrise Dancer. Gets every chance from the inside draw. Respect any strong moves in the market. SCOTT SALISH (4) produced a moderate effort last time when fifth at Shepparton over 450m behind Toss It Up (26.24) in a Maiden. Was in the money the start prior. Comes out of a solid form race last start. Expected to feature in the finish. IT AND BIT (6) has gone well at his last couple of runs here, most recently when third beaten 5 lengths (17.39). Overdue and expected to feature again. JUMBUK SHENZHEN (8) is a newcomer from the Gary Joske kennel. Start all important and will need some luck getting across from the wide draw. Respect any moves in the market.",
